Actually, it's not too hard. 

Have a second DNS A record added for the new name

Change the reverse (PTR) record changed to the new name.

/usr/sbin/netsetup and /usr/sbin/mailsetup 

If you are using NIS, you will probably also have to do a ypsetup. 

That should do most everything. Reboot the system and you
should be there. Once everyone knows about the change (if anyone
cares), have the old A record deleted from the DNS zone file. Viola!

I last did this about 6 months ago, so I may have missed something,
but I don't think so.
