From: Geoff Allen <geoff@wsu.edu>
Subject: Strange behavior from Decstation 5000/25
Date: 1997/07/29
Message-ID: <u3u3hd4jqn.fsf@cyclone.it.wsu.edu>#1/1
X-Deja-AN: 260312703
Organization: Professional Unix Geek, Washington State University
Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


I've got a Decstation 5000/25 that's been driving me crazy recently,
and I wonder if anyone else might have some insight to share.

The system had ULTRIX 4.4 installed, and was having some problems (out
of swap, to be exact), so I did a shutdown -r to reboot it. It
wouldn't boot after that. I could boot off of the ULTRIX CD-ROM, but
not from the disk.

Called DEC and reported the symptoms (see below for details). DEC
said, "It sounds like your kernel's corrupt; try genvmunix." Well, I
didn't have a genvmunix. Harumph. So I re-installed.

The system was fine, until the next time I did a shutdown, at which
point I had exactly the same problem. Aha! It must be hardware! So, we
called the hardware support guys. They replaced everything, one piece
at a time, with no success. (Not that that's a whole lot -- memory,
processor card, motherboard, power supply.) Also tried different SCSI
cables, booting with and without the monitor, keyboard, etc. Nothing
changed things, so I suspected a corrupt disk. Borrowed another disk
and installed onto it. Everything worked fine until the NEXT time I
shut the system down. Now guess what? It won't boot. And this time I
have a genvmunix, but it won't boot, either. The only thing that will
boot is the CD-ROM.

Here's what it does when booting from any of the three kernels (4.5
vmunix, 4.5 genvmunix, and 4.4 vmunix) that I now have on two
different disks:

	Goes OK through the hardware checks
	Bootstraps the kernel
	Starts finding/listing hardware, to the following point:

		fs0 at ibus3
		dti0 at ibus3
		fb0 at ibus3
		fb: Module type PMAG-DV  1024x768

	at this point, it echos a line feed (with no carriage return,
	so the cursor is below the space after "768"), there is a
	beep, and the keyboard LEDs flash, but nothing ever happens
	after this.

When I boot from the CD-ROM, the same general things happen, but after
the beep and keyboard LEDs flash, it pauses for about 10 seconds and
then gives me the Installation/System Maintenance menu.

If the problem were something corrupting the kernel, I'd expect
genvmunix to still be ok.  So on the theory that maybe something was
corrupting the filesystems at shutdown, I went into the system
maintenance shell off the CD-ROM and did an fsck of the / and /usr
partitions from the hard disk ("summary info bad" was the only problem
found and fixed), followed by "halt -n" and boot off the hard disk. No
luck.

If anybody has any idea what might be wrong and how to fix it, I'd
love to hear from you! Re-installing after every reboot/shutdown is
kind of a pain.

Geoff

