stefan.osterman@upnet.se wrote:
> 
> Which is the easiest way to change the hostname, without having
> to change all the license keys and everything.
> 
> I use DEC Unix 4.0b

Use 'hostname.'  Easiest thing to do is change it in /etc/rc.config,
then reboot.  DEC licenses are keyed off of the system hardware id (see
sysconfig(2), not the host name.  Most other vendor's license work
the same way, but check with your vendor to be sure.
-- 
