Most Unix OS's I've played with don't allow login to root from
a networked connection. It's a security thing. It's too easy for
a hacker to distroy your system if he can get into root, and most
hackers nowadays come in through the internet.

If you really need to log into root, you should look into programs
such as 'sudo' and 'su', and implement as much of the security as
you can stand.




