> 
> Which is the easiest way to change the hostname, without having
> to change all the license keys and everything.
> 
Hi Stefan.

Now, to answer your question. Actually, there are two names, machine
name and host name.

Machine name is assigned during the instalation and is somewhat dificult
to change. That name refers to (among other) the configuration files for
your current kernel build (ouch!). It is also refernced by several other
processes/daemons.

Host name is tha name of your machine on network. It simply maps name
into IP address and is used by all network commands. Discrepancy between
these two names is dangerous and sometimes fatal (if network is vital to
the machine).

I'm not sure, but you cantry command hostname, perhaps it can change the
host name. Frankly, I doubt it. Machine/Host name is something
fundamental to that particular instance of Digital UNIX and I don't
think you can change it easily. With the expertize I have I could try
it, but I wouldn't guarantee success.

The cleanest way is to re-install, I'm afraid.

I hope I've helped you. Don't take my oppinion as final, ask some more,
dig into it.

Wish you luck,
Nix.
