On our site, we have a VAX server running VMS 5.5-2. After upgrading from 
Pathwork 4.2 to Pathwork 5.0e, we are trying to solve these security problems:
In version 4.2, every user should identify himself in order to get full 
access rights to his acount. He couldn't make a network connection (By using
the DOS command: USE ?: \\SERVER\Username) without knowing the password.
Now the situation is this: If a user has a "USER" privilege level, he's in a
strange situation - He can be mapped to his account, but cannot make any action
- read, write, delete - on the mapped driver. While trying, he gets error 
messages like "Access denied", etc...
If we give him the "ADMIN" privilege level, he can do everything, include 
mapping to any account he wants, without be forced to recognize himself!!!
Of course it's not what we want!!

On our system, every Pathwork user is a VAX user also.
We have noticed that every new acount, no matter if it was created automticaly
when we installed Pathwork 5.0 or was opened later, has a "Personal share" 
with the name of the user and his root directory. While zooming on the shared 
resource, we see that the owner & system has WRE rights, and group & world
has none. As i 've already mentioned, that doesn't effect the unconditioned
mapping.
Can somebody give me any help or hints?

