In article <33D4DDBD.68C2@cae.ca>, Steven Geller <steven@cae.ca> writes...
>We will be using a workstation based on DECs DMCC PICMG Alpha card (Unix
>OS) and 14-slot PCI/ISA passive backplane.  Our application requires
>multiple (at least three) video/graphics controller cards to operate
>simultaneously from a single workstation and drive independant monitors.
	It should work.  Its been tested & seen to work.  Ideally your FAE
	can help.

>Are there any limitations or special/unique configuration set-up
>procedures to ensure that the above arrangement will operate as
>required?
	Officially, Digital UNIX supports upto 3 graphics heads using TGA2
	(i.e. Powerstorm 3D30).  There are specific issues when the cards are
	in the  secondary slots.  The first graphics head _needs_ to be in the
	primary slot.  VGAEN jumper needs to be _in_ for the primary card and
	out for all other graphics cards.  DMA needs to be disabled.

	Make sure the same graphics cards are used, all resolutions setting on 
	each card should be the same. 

	It needs some care to get it running.

