fstarr@polymer.bu.edu wrote:
> 
> I need to boot my new DEC AU500 into single user mode, because
> I have some network problems.  Unfortunately, I cannot find any
> way to do this.
> 
> Does anyone know how to boot into sinlge user mode WITHOUT first
> going into multi-user mode??  There appears to be no ROM prompt.
> 
> Thanks for your help.
> 
>         Francis Starr

When the system starts auto-boot (in about 2 seconds time frame) press
<Ctrl+C>. You should get the FirmWare prompt (it is >>>). Then boot your
system with:

boot -flags s

and you'll boot your Digital UNIX or OSF/1 in single user mode.

