Newsgroups: comp.sys.dec


I have had a problem with a couple of PW 433a's with 10/100baseT network
cards running WinNT 4.0 ever since I got them in April.  They would lose
the DHCP lease at least every other day.  A full power-down is required
to reset the card.  This was almost always while PRO/Engineer (a
computer intensive MCAD program) was running.  I got a new driver from
DEC that was supposed to fix this, but it never made much difference.  I
had the card replaced in one of the machines when it was slow to respond
to a network analyizer during a DEC service call, but it didn't really
make a difference.

In the last few days, I have been losing the network 8-9 times a day. 
Often the computer is just sitting there with normal network traffic
when it happens. I loaded Service Pack 3 thinking that it might help. 
No difference.  The error from the Event Viewer is usually as follows:

"DHCP failed to renew a lease for the card with network address
0000F8752915. The following error occurred : 
The semaphore timeout period has expired."

I just replaced the card with the 10baseT card that came with the
computer and it seems to be working right now.

Does anyone have any suggestions on what might be causing my grief?

Thanks,

Doug Burstedt
dburstedt@src.uniden.com
Uniden San Diego Research Center



