Matt,

Did you buy a classic Pentium 166 for a Venturis with a Socket 7, or a
Pentium OverDrive 166 for a Venturis with a Socket 5.  If the latter,
the programmers(s) of the BIOS never anticipated a speed > 133 MHz,
and the BIOS reports 133MHz.  Programmers as a breed are a woefully
shortsighted lot.

Make sure the CPU bus speed is jumpered for 66MHz.  Then download Ray
Van Tassel's shareware CACHECHK utility.  It also reports the CPU
speed accurately.  So does a program from Intel called CPUSPEED, but
only for the Pentium, of course.

You can find CACHECHK at http://www.shareware.com and CPUSPEED at
http://www.intel.com

... Ben Myers

