Actually, you have the sign reversed; almost any DIGITAL Alpha
system that runs Digital UNIX will run NT, not the other way around.

The set of hardware supported under UNIX is generally smaller
than under NT (e.g. graphics accelarators).

So some care is required; check carefully your machine configuration
before ordering (one way that generally works is to order the
UNIX variant of the system, which is obviously configured validly
for Digital UNIX.
