>I am currently having serious problems with one of my Dec 3000/300
>Alpha machines. The system will not spin up the hard drives or show any
>messages on the monitor. The LED lights all come on at power up, but
>then the code 01011111 is displayed on the LED's. I have indicated the
>code by starting with the LED closest to the back of the machine.
>
>I have tried a different system hard drive which I know is good on 
>this system but the problem still exists. I have also swapped memory and
>SCSI cables with a good system but with no results. If anyone has
>the service guide for the 3000/300 system that lists these LED error
>codes, I'd appreciate you passing them along. 

Actually, they read left to right, so it's 1111 1010, or FC.  
According to my hardware reference guide (EK-PELCN-OG. C01), F0 - FF and
20 indicate a "category of code" of the SROM power-up sequence.

According to the same manual, the SROM code tests memory sizing, I/O,
and cache.  Without seeing the service guide to know exactly what's broken,
I would concur that it's probably a motherboard problem, but then again,
that's like calling an oil leak a car problem.  
 
