Thomas G Sweat Jr wrote:
> Due to some legal situations I need to completely wipe several files
> from my RAID system in a fashion that will make them unrecoverable.

It doesn't look like NT has a delete/erase command.  Perhaps you
could delete the file from a command prompt and then fill all 
remaining space on the disk with trash until there are zero 
bytes left, thereby ensuring that the file has been written over.

    echo off
    :doit
       copy little1+big1 big2 > NUL
       copy little1+big2 big1 > NUL
       dir | findstr free
    goto doit
    
Fancier versions of the above are certainly possible.

Are you also obligated to erase all backups?

	/john



