Kevin,

I don't know the Starion at all.  Look inside the case.  See if the
CPU socket is labeled "Socket 5" or "Socket 7".  If it's a Socket 5,
you need a Pentium OverDrive processor or an adapter that handles the
Socket 5 to Socket 7 conversion.  Also, check the Starion manual or
the jumpers on the motherboard.  Look for one set of jumper (maybe
even labeled on the motherboard would be nice) that changes the
external system bus clock among 50, 60, and 66MHz.  Right now your
external system bus clock is 50MHz.  Then look for jumpers to set the
CPU clock multiplier.  Typical multipliers are 1.5 and 2 for Socket 5,
1.5, 2, 2.5, and 3 for Socket 7.

The clock multiplier jumper setting times the external bus clock speed
drives the CPU at its rated clock speed (or even overclocks it),
Pentium OverDrives excepted... Ben Myers

