Silverpike wrote:
> 
> I have found that on an AlphaStation 500 (333 MHz), the DEC CPU-PCI bridge
> violates bus protocol.  Whenever a target signals a target-abort when the
> bridge is the initiator, it throws an exception and halts the system.  If it
> is relevant, I am running Win NT 4.0 Workstation on it.
> 
> I am wondering if there is a way around this.  The system should not halt on a
> target-abort, as they are non-fatal errors.  Anyone with any helpful
> information please respond as this presents me a significant problem.
> 

There are a several protocols for target termination on PCI - are you
sure you mean target abort? The PCI spec, section 3.3.2 says:

"Target Abort refers to an abnormal termination requested because the
target
    detected a fatal error or the target will never be able to complete
the
    request. "

What application and PCI devices are you expecting to use target abort
and
continue running?

