Shawn Dillon wrote:
> 
> Hi,
>         I have a Digital 5100 Prioris server that HAD 64 MB of RAM . I upgraded
> the server with a 64MB kit , to 128 MB . The BIOS recognizes the memory
> addition , bu t Windows NT Server 4.0 fails to see the total 128MB RAM . It
> reports only 65 MB of RAM.
> 
> Has anyone seen this situation before? I upgraded the BIOS , and still no
> answer. Any help wpuld be greatly appreciated...

Run the System Configuration Utility (SCU) and make sure the
memory is seen there, *SAVE* the settings, exit and reboot.

Always with an EISA machine if you change the configuration
(add/remove memory/boards) run the SCU (formerly also often
known as the ECU, EISA Configuration Utility).

Once you've done that, I'm sure NT will see the memory just
fine (if it doesn't *THEN* you have a problem with the
memory ;-).

