In article <01bc8dea$b61c6870$0102f8cb@ns>, "centis" <centis@cnts.co.kr> writes:
:Does  DEC8400 support DDS-3?

  The literal answer -- though I don't think it's what you meant to ask:
  with the configuration of a SCSI DDS DAT drive that supports the DDS-3
  recording format, yes, the AlphaServer 8400 series -- and any other
  computer system with generic SCSI tape support -- can support DDS-3.

	--

  There are presently no announced DDS-3 DAT drive products available
  from Digital, however. DDS-2 drives, DDS-2 loaders, and AIT and DLT
  drives are available.

  The TLZ9L loader has 32 and 64 GB capacity, and 775 and 1550 kilobytes
  per second transfer.  The values are native and compressed, respectively.

  The drive between Digital's current DAT and DLT offerings is the TZS20
  (25 and 50GB capacity, 3 and 6MB per second transfer rate.  Values are
  native and compressed, respectively) "Advanced Intelligent Tape" (AIT)
  tape drive.

  The TZ89 DLT drive has 35 and 70 GB capacity.  Loaders for various DLT
  drives are available, as well.

