>I have a DEC3000/400S which has run out of expansion capabilities so I
>have
>tried to install a PMAZC-AA TurboChannel SCSI controller in slot zero in
>order that I can attach a BA356 storageworks shelf.
>
>The system as it currently stands has SCSI buses A and B; A is the
>internal
>SCSI bus and B controls a BA350 shelf. If I run the self test on the
>PMAZC-AA _without_ the BA356 connected the card checks out fine, but as
>soon as I power on the BA356 and run the self tests I get a NINQ error
>(nondma enquiry failure).
>
>I think the trick is to get "show device" and "t tc0 cnfg" to see the
>controller as SCSI buses C and D, but I have so far been unsuccessful.
>
>Has anyone else experienced similar problems? If so I would be grateful
>for
>any assistaqnce you can offer. Please reply by e-mail to sb@m4.net
>
>Cheers,
>Steven Berry.

I'm not sure about the error, but you will not get the TC cards to be
higher than the on board devices. That is the one thing I never liked
about those machines. The devices will be named by TC adapter (TC0,
TC1, TC2, main board=TC3) and the motherboard is the highest TC
adapter, so it will always be the last controller. It makes these
machines painful to add disk space to unless logicals have been
faithfully used, or the system disk can be moved to a different bus. 

As far as the PMAGC, that is the dual SCSI controller, correct? Do you
have both channels properly terminated. The BA356 should have its own
termination if properly configured, is the other port terminated?
Active termination is recommended. How long is the cable connecting
the two new devices? The BA356 has lots of internal cable length as I
recall.

Good Luck,

Steve



