Sounds more like badly configured and over-indulgence in network protocols.

For a start, stick to a common protocol, ie TCP/IP or IPX.

Make absolutely sure that the protocols you decide upon are bound to the
network adaptor.  

Its sounds quite likely, but not necessarily so, that mulliple protocols
are being used and incorrect bindings are being set (or the correct
bindings are being used and not configured correctly). 

Don't use DNS. 

Only use an automatic DHCP on the server.

Set clients to accept auto DHCP settings.

Set client to either accept auto DHCP settings for WINS or set a hard
address for WINS.

Make sure you allow NETBIOS support over TCP/IP.

