In article <33C247FA.6C46@hugo.rz.fh-ulm.de>,
IE1 Joachim Mueller  <JOAMUELL@hugo.rz.fh-ulm.de> wrote:
>
>In the two cabinets are after removing the frontpanel some connectors 
>for harddisks. Which type of harddisk do I have to use?
>(Perhaps ESDI). And which sort of controller should I have to choose
>for the disks?. There is only one quad controller for some big
>harddisks, originally shipped with this machine.


This is the distribution panel from an RQDX3 , an MFM controller. 
You should notice a very wide ribbon cable  going from the panel
to the controller board itself,  somehwere else on the bus. 
Anyways, the device will control  up to 4 MFM drives. If you want to
spend some time entering drive geometry for exotic devices by hand,
then you can use a lot of things, but generally speaking, youll need
an RD52, RD53, or RD54. (30, 71, and 159 megs respectively)
These were dec's numbers for various offerings by seagate and Micropolis
and theyre failry common ( or used to be).. You might want to look
for an ESDI controller ( or a DSSI  board, but that smells expensive)
and toss in a large ESDI drive, but again, theres the problem of 
where to find such a thing. SCSI to Q bus adapters werent very common
and while they can be found, theyre not usualy to be found cheaply,
since this is about th eonly way to more or less be sure you can 
keep your uVax  in a supply of useable working disks into the future.. 

anwyays.. ask around for some RD53's or 54's. somebody will have one. 

Isildur



