> Does anyone have jumper specs for an RZ25-E?
>
> I just picked up a refurbished one and need to know which
> jumper controls termination.  (The termpacks are surface-mounted,
> so unless the thing is ALWAYS terminated or autosensing, which
> are both unlikely, a jumper(s) should switch them in and out.
>
> Can you help me out?
>
> (I've scoured DEC's site, and other fonts of knowledge, and have
> found the SCSI ID jumpers and spinup jumpers, but nothing
> regarding termination)
>
> Thanks in advance for anything you can turn up!
>
> -DanD

The following information is NOT guaranteed or warranteed, but I believe
it is correct.

  The drive kit shall include a SCSI terminating pack which consists
      of (3) 220/330 ohm resistor packs. Terminating resistors are
networks
      of resistors that terminate the SCSI bus.  The last physical SCSI
      device connected to the SCSI interface cable must be terminated.
      Therefore, termination must be done within the drive.  Please note
that
      SCSI terminators are not required for those devices with end of
cable
      terminators or external terminators.  If required, the (3)
terminator
      resistor packs need to be installed by the user just behind the
SCSI port
      connector.

 JUMPER BLOCK J6

   POSITION     USE                                     CONFIGURATION
          P1       Self test for factory use only          OUT(1)
       P2       Spin up on power application            OUT (2)
       P2       Wait for spin up command                IN (2)
       P3       Not for use                             OUT(1)
       P4       Write protect                           OUT(1)
       P5       Parity checking enabled                 IN(1)
       P6       Reserved for later use                  OUT(1)
       P7       Drive supplies power to the SCSI bus    IN(1)
       P8       Power to drive internal terminators     IN(1)
--
----------------------------------------------------------
The above is MY opinion only... and NOT a response from Digital
Equipment Corp.

