My name is Greg Earle.  I'm the Usenet newsmaster at the
Jet Propulsion Laboratory.

The following article was a forgery, posted by someone in Canada who
apparently wanted to have people connect to their Web server at
http://www.tripod.com/, for whatever reason.  It's plain to see that
this article originated at the host ts35-10.Ott.IStar.CA, from the
NNTP-Posting-Host: header and the Path: header.

I'd like to apologize to anyone who was mislead by this forgery, and more
importantly I would like to emphasize that JPL is not in any way adding
additional mirrors to our sites without explicit notification of same
on our existing Web servers.

I'm cc'ing this post to JPL's security group as well as the Postmaster of
IStar.CA, to inform them that we do not tolerate this sort of activity.

Questions regarding this post can be directed to me at the address below.

