There is more to a computer than the CPU chip.  Just because there is no
difference in the actual DECchip 21x64 chips doesn't mean that any specific
OS will work on any system that uses them.  The curent models in the PWS-au
series will, evidently, never run VMS (at least not outside of their lab).
This fall they are due for what has been called a "re-spin" - I expect that
this means a redesign, using some different components; it is this redesigned
PWS-au which is supposed to support/be supported by VMS.

The main reasons for the various incompatabilities that exist are things
lacking in the firmware, particularly the PAL code and the consoles, and
also some memory management and, if I recall correctly, timing problems.

--- Carl



