The processor cabinet is around 400 lb (182 kg), and is 41.8" high x 30"
deep x 29" wide.  The width can be a bit tricky for a standard
residential door.

>If you're thinking about putting a Vax 11/750 into your house, you
>had better think twice about it.  The main system cabinet is about
>as tall as a washing machine, but wider.  Then you need space
>for disk drives, same height but narrower.  Then you've got power

It is true that it is not easy (or for the faint of heart) but it can be
done.  I am posting this from an 11/750 system that I have at home.

>considerations.  Can you say 3-phase power?  And then you get
>to cool off all that electricity you're using. Don't forget some tape
>drives too.

3-phase??  No.  It is single phase, either 110 or 220 V.  Power is around
1.7 kW max. and you will need a twist-and-lock (Hubble) receptacle.
Cooling can be a serious problem.  Figure that it will add 10-15 degrees
F to a well ventillated room.  An open basement would be a better choice
than a den.

