To be fair to Digital, the company prices its products according to what
it costs them to produce the product. In the case of a WNT-based
AlphaServer, DEC forks over a minimum of $600 to Micro$oft for each copy
of NTAS. In the case of OVMS or Digital UNIX, the amortized cost of the
OSes apparently is significantly higher than $600 per system.

That being said, restricting, artificially or otherwise, certain Alpha
chips to certain OSes blows a way-huge hole in the "Universal Platform"
Alpha value proposition, no?

Cheers,

Terry Shannon



