In general, if you wish to run WindowsNT, D-UNIX and/or OpenVMS on the
Alpha, stick to DEC drives.  The issue is the same as network cards,
video cards, etc.....namely, cross-operating system availability of
drivers.  For example, the AlphaStation400 used to ship, by default
with the DEC ZLxP-e1 video card instead of a card such at Diamond
Viper, Stealth, etc....since DEC would support the ZLxP-e1, e2 and e3
cards with drivers for all 3 operating systems in a switchable-boot
configuration.

I have an AlphaStation400 with two DEC RZ-series drives and one Seagate
drive.  This combination has worked under WindowsNT for about 2 years
now.  I can say that I have been impressed with the overall performance
and continuous throughput of DEC's SCSI drives.

Hope this helps...





