   Steven Berry wrote:
   > You use the disklabel command to partition the disk (up to 8
   > partitions
   > allowed) and the newfs command to create a filesystem on a device.

   Been there, done that.

   The disklabel and newfs commands only partition the drive and create
   filesystems on it.  They do NOT do bad block forwarding.

   What I'm looking for is something like the Solaris "format ... analyze"
   or the old "bad144" commands.  Any help?


I'm afraid I missed the beginning of this thread, but if you are
talking about Digital Unix, I think you can do this with the "scu"
program ("SCSI CAM Utility").  There is an extensive man page, in
