I always thought that "RC" stood for "Resin Coated'.   :-)

There were exactly three differences between the VAXstation II/RC and
and the non-RC model:

1) Expoxy cement in the last three slots of the 8-slot backplane.

2) The expansion memory board was 2MB instead of 1MB (yes, more memory).

3) The price was $10,000 less ($15,000 instead of $25,000).

Oh, there was one other minor difference: the medallion had 
"/RC" added to it.

My II/RC long ago migrated into a BA123 cabinet, and has received
many updates over the years.   Now the only original part is the
CPU board.   It is still in daily use (I am typing this note on it).

