> specialized in replacement backplanes.

This was because DEC stopped selling replacement H9278-A backplanes
that week.   I got my order in before the cutoff, but had to argue
with them to get it shipped.   Zoltech was already making backplanes
(identical in size/shape to the H9278-A) for their own systems, so
this was a happy event for them.   The Zoltech backplanes also had
tapered openings for the card slots, so it was much easier to insert
cards.

