Note 1451.0             A Field Guide to DEC SCSI Cables               7 replies
EISNER::KENNEDY "Terry Kennedy"                      49 lines  29-JUN-1993 21:22
--------------------------------------------------------------------------------
  The following may be useful to people trying to buy SCSI cables from DEC,
since the "Cables" section of the DECdirect hardware catalog has become
smaller and smaller, the Electronic Connection's "Cable Configurator" is a
joke, and because two out of 3 calls I placed to DECdirect "Technical Con-
sulting" gave the wrong answer(s).

  DEC equipment has 3 kinds of external SCSI connectors, two of which are
also found on industry-standard units.

  68-pin high-density connector - this is used on the VAXstation 3100 and
	systems with low-end SCSI. The male connector is on the system, and
	the female connector is on the cable. This format is peculiar to DEC.
	Called 68HD-F in tables below.

  50-pin high-density connector - this is used on the DECstation product line
	and on systems with high-end SCSI. Connector gender is reversed from
	the above - mail connector on the cable, female on the system. This
	format is often used on industry-standard systems. Called 50HD-M in
	tables below.

  50-pin "Centronics" connector (actually, it isn't - it's an Amphenol 50-pin
	"telco" connector, while Centronics is a 36-pin flavor, but the name
	stuck - this is the traditional SCSI connector, with male connectors
	on the cable and female ones on the option. Called 50C-M in tables
	below.

  50-pin "DB50" connector (likewise, it isn't - it's a C format) - DEC doesn't
	use this style and I believe it is peculiar to older Sun systems. Not
	listed in tables below as DEC doesn't make this style.

End "A"  End "B"  Length   BC-number  17-number
-------  -------  -------  ---------  -----------
68HD-F   50C-M    3 feet   BC56H-03   Unknown
68HD-F   50C-M    6 feet   BC56H-06   Unknown
68HD-F   50C-M    9 feet   BC56H-09   Unknown
50HD-M   50C-M    3 feet   BC09D-03   17-02641-01
50HD-M   50C-M    6 feet   BC09D-06   17-02641-02
50HD-M   50C-M    12 feet  BC09D-12   Unknown
50C-M    50C-M    18 inch  BC19J-1E   17-01351-04
50C-M    50C-M    3 feet   BC19J-03   17-01351-01
50C-M    50C-M    6 feet   BC19J-06   17-01351-02
50C-M    50C-M    9 feet   Unknown    17-01351-03

  Also, the 50C-M SCSI terminator is H8574-A / 12-30552-01.

  Note that because of the stupid games DEC is playing to create the illusion
of "street pricing", you should check the price of both the normal number and
the 17-number for these cables, as you will find different pricing as well as
the fact that your discount may apply one way but not the other.



