  You don't need a TK Driver for DOS/Windows.

The TZK is a SCSI tape drive so connect it to the scsi bus with a free
scsi id.  Check by booting the system and making sure that the device is
seen at free id.  Now, check the instructions for the BACKUP S/W you are
using.  Make sure that it supports a SCSI tape device (MS-Backup does
not).  Sometimes the backup s/w requires that the ASPI SCSI driver is
loaded (seagate backup requires this) in config.sys.

I have used the drive on both adapetc and NCR SCSI controllers with no
problems.

Jeff

